# MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT — ApplyEase
## University Application Workflow Automation Platform

Act as a senior full-stack software architect, senior Next.js engineer, Supabase specialist, database designer, UI/UX designer, application security engineer, and QA engineer.

Build **ApplyEase**, a complete, production-oriented, full-stack university application management and workflow automation platform. The platform will digitize university administrative processes, eliminate unnecessary paperwork, automate approval workflows, enable electronic signing and stamping, track application progress in real time, and hold responsible staff accountable for missed processing deadlines.

Do not build a static prototype, a collection of disconnected dashboard screens, or a frontend-only demonstration. Build a functional application with persistent database storage, secure authentication, real authorization, working forms, real workflow transitions, file uploads, notifications, audit trails, and end-to-end application processing.

When a feature depends on external credentials or a paid provider, implement the appropriate integration boundary and a working development alternative. Never represent a simulated operation as a completed real-world action.

